# Beyond UI – Components and Styling

- **ALWAYS use Beyond UI components** from `@unicornlove/beyond-ui` when creating or updating UI.
- **SOURCE design tokens** from the Beyond UI package (see `packages/beyond-ui` themes/tokens); do not invent new colors or spacing values.
- **Use theme variables** instead of hardcoded colors; prefer semantic tokens for consistency.

## References

- [API conventions](packages/beyond-ui/docs/API_CONVENTIONS.md) – Prop naming and style factories.
- [STYLING_GUIDE](packages/beyond-ui/STYLING_GUIDE.md) – Tokens and styling patterns.

## Best practices

1. Use theme/token variables instead of hardcoded colors.
2. Prefer Beyond UI layout primitives (Stack, Row, Grid, Box) and components.
3. Keep styles consistent with the design system defined in the Beyond UI package.
